# Every variable this gateway reads, and only those. The three with no default
# are the three it refuses to start without: each names something it cannot
# function without — somewhere to reach, or the name it composes endpoint keys
# from — and defaulting any of them produces a process that starts, answers
# /health, and does nothing it exists to do.
#
# Two of the three are read only where the gateway evaluates, so
# RAIL_TICKET_MODE=none starts without them.

# Where admitted calls go. Required, in every mode.
RAIL_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM_URL=

# Where the policy bundle comes from. Required unless RAIL_TICKET_MODE=none,
# which fetches no bundle and does not read this. The route beneath it is the
# OpenAPI specification's, so what a deployment configures is the origin alone.
RAIL_CENTER_URL=

# The data source this gateway fronts, and the first segment of every endpoint
# key it composes: `delivery` makes `delivery.track_package`. Required unless
# RAIL_TICKET_MODE=none. It must be the slug the data source was registered
# under, because that is what Rail Center keys the bundle's bindings on — a
# deployment that gets it wrong composes keys matching no binding, and what that
# costs is the bundle's to say: under a `pass` fallback every endpoint faces the
# whole chain, and under `block` every call is refused.
RAIL_DATASOURCE_SLUG=

# Whether this gateway has a control plane: none | plugin. Default plugin, so a
# deployment that forgets the line asks Rail Center what to do rather than
# deciding for itself to have none. Platform-wide rather than this component's
# own — the proxy in front reads the same variable — so case is folded and one
# value configures a whole zone.
#
# It does NOT say how much of a decision is acted on. That is the bundle's
# `enforcement` posture, and it arrives on every poll, so moving a gateway
# between judging nothing, reporting and refusing is a change in Rail Center
# rather than a redeploy. `observe` and `enforce` were values of this variable
# and are refused at startup now, with a message naming where the posture went;
# so is anything else.
RAIL_TICKET_MODE=

# The credential presented to Rail Center: none | bearer. `gcp` is named by the
# platform contract and refused by this component under its own name rather
# than as an unknown mode. RAIL_AUTH_TOKEN is required when the mode is bearer
# and unread otherwise.
RAIL_AUTH_MODE=
RAIL_AUTH_TOKEN=

# How often to ask Rail Center for the bundle again, in seconds. Default 60,
# floor 5 — a value below the floor is raised to it with a warning rather than
# refused, since an interval that is merely too eager is not worth taking
# enforcement down over.
RAIL_GATEWAY_BUNDLE_REFRESH_SECONDS=

# Default 8080.
RAIL_GATEWAY_PORT=

# CRITICAL | ERROR | WARNING | INFO | DEBUG. Default INFO.
RAIL_GATEWAY_LOG_LEVEL=
